    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d234">

                <pb facs="0514" n="482" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v19/pg482"/>

                <head>234. Telegram From the Embassy in Poland to the Department of State<anchor
                        n="0" xml:id="d234-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Warsaw</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-11-07T17:00:00+01:00">November 7, 1958,
                            5 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>696. USUN information for Lodge. Beam–Wang Talks.</p>
                <p>83rd meeting one hour forty minutes.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d234-f2"/> Wang led off
                    with brief statement protesting alleged use US-supplied poison gas by GRC and
                    demanding discussion US withdrawal from Taiwan area. I responded with sharp
                    attack on ChiCom shelling Quemoy and concocting of poison gas charge along lines
                    Deptel 560.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d234-f3"/> Wang then read lengthy statement
                    making <pb facs="0515" n="483" xml:id="pg483"/> usual accusations US interfering
                    in Chinese internal affairs and endeavoring create two Chinas. I responded with
                    material showing international character of dispute and drawing analogy to
                    situation other divided countries as set forth reference telegram. Wang replied
                    denying applicability of analogy and in rather abusive language charging US
                    continuing practice provoking civil war in China which it had engaged in for
                    past century. I rebuked Wang for abusiveness of language following which he
                    somewhat milder but that nothing new to offer. I proposed next meeting Tuesday
                    November 25, 2 p.m. to which Wang agreed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Beam</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d234-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d234-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 611.93/11–758. Secret; Priority;
                    Limit Distribution. Repeated to USUN and Taipei.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d234-f2" n="1" xml:id="d234-f2-content">
                <p>Beam sent a detailed report of the meeting in telegram 697 from Warsaw, November
                    7, and his comments and recommendations in telegram 703 from Warsaw, November 8.
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Ibid.,</hi> 611.93/11–758 and 611.93/11–858,
                    respectively; see Supplement)</p>
            </note>
